#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# through

#% text
# `through(p(f, g, ...)(x))` gives `p(f(x), g(x), ...)`: each function of the head applied to the arguments.

#% text
# `through(e, p)` does so only when the inner head is `p`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The result is evaluated; a term whose head is not a call is left as it is.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
through(p(f, g)(x))
#% output
#= p(f(x), g(x))

#% cell
through([sin, cos](0.5))
#% output
#= [0.479425538604203, 0.8775825618903728]

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Only for one head:

#% cell
through(p(f, g)(x), q)
#% output
#= p(f, g)(x)

#% subsection
# Applications

#% text
# Several statistics of one list:

#% cell
through([min, max, mean]([3, 1, 4, 1, 5]))
#% output
#= [1, 5, 14/5]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `map`, `composition`, `apply`
